id: pm-e2bq
title: "Tiered contracts-driven help: one-screen core help, full surface via pm help --all, generated from the contract table"
description: "Default pm --help shows only the ~15 canonical nouns; pm help --all (and --explain) reveals the full surface incl. deprecated aliases; both views plus completions and docs command tables are generated from sdk/cli-contracts so help can never drift from contracts. Duplicate check: pm-5k2w (closed) trimmed help alias bloat once; no generated-tiered-help item exists."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:35.309Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T22:52:02.619Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-26T22:51:42.554Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-26T22:51:42.554Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: pm --help renders one screen listing canonical nouns only; pm help --all lists everything incl. aliases marked deprecated; help/completions/docs command tables generated from the contract table with a drift gate; after-measurement (pm-a22j script) shows reduced default help + contracts token cost
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: implemented
expected_result: Default help remains compact while explicit full discovery exposes the complete command and deprecated alias surface from runtime contracts.
actual_result: Default/full structured help exposes 14/69 subcommands and 23 lifecycle-described aliases; package lifecycle exposes 15 subcommands and all gates pass.
