comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T21:27:35.154Z","harness:codex","GitHub intake: GH-1127 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1127. Reused the exact tiered-help feature. Red reproduction: default help intentionally stays at 14 canonical commands, but pm help --all is not declared and still returns only the same 14-command view instead of the complete standard/full surface."
  "2026-08-26T21:34:27.309Z","harness:codex","TDD red: help presentation and structured-help specs prove --all still filters to core commands and does not expose deprecated alias lifecycle metadata."
  "2026-08-26T22:51:37.953Z","harness:codex","Evidence: root help is now tiered: fresh-directory structured acceptance exposed 14 default subcommands versus 69 with --all, plus 23 lifecycle-described command aliases; package help exposed 15 lifecycle subcommands including install and upgrade. The linked sandbox-safe suite passed 239/239. Repository gates passed pnpm build, pnpm lint, zero jscpd clones, command grammar 164/164, flag parity 2839/2839, 584 files and 8025 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, pnpm audit clean, and Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vuln+secret+misconfig clean."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T22:51:38.552Z","harness:codex",A compact default help surface and an explicit full-discovery surface can share one command registry when visibility selection is centralized and structured help carries alias lifecycle metadata.
